  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$ and $10 B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & \\alpha \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]$\r\nIf $B$ is the inverse of $A$, then the value of $\\alpha$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\r\n4\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n3\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$-4$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n5",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$\r\n$\\therefore|A|=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$\r\n$=1(1+3)+1(2+3)+1(2-1)=4+5+1=10$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\operatorname{Adj} A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}4 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3\\end{array}\\right]^T=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad B=A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\left[\\because A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{|A|} \\operatorname{Adj} A\\right]$\r\n$\\Rightarrow 10 B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]$\r\nHence, $\\alpha=5$"
  }
}